# What Vercel does not need to build or serve the app.
#
# This is an upload filter, nothing more — it does not delete anything and it
# does not apply to the BigRock runner, which gets the whole project
# (DEPLOY.md §2, Option 1). Everything excluded here is either a development
# tool or deployed somewhere else.
#
# Every pattern is anchored with a leading slash. Without it these match at
# any depth the way .gitignore does, so a bare `docs/` also drops `lib/docs/`
# and `app/(app)/docs/`, and the build fails on Vercel but not locally.
#
# `scripts/`, `runner/` and `jobs/` are deliberately NOT here. The runner is
# the background queue BigRock's cron drives every five minutes, and the
# scripts are the firm's own operational tools — `npm run doctor`,
# `npm run jobs:tick`, `npm run purge:sample`, `npm run opinions:empty`.

# the test suites and their output
/tests/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/playwright.config.mjs
/vitest.config.mjs
/.env.test

# written for people, not for the server
/docs/

# the PHP file gateway: deployed to BigRock cPanel, never to Vercel
# (docs/GATEWAY_DEPLOY.md)
/gateway/
/docker-compose.gateway.yml

# local file vaults, if a dev run left one behind
/.storage/
/.storage-test/
/.gateway-local/
